<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>纽约时报 &amp;gt; 美国 &amp;gt; 政治</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/spotlight/on-politics</link><description></description><lastBuildDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 23:24:14 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>特朗普如何疏远共和党选民</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/08/us/politics/trump-republican-voters.html</link><description>另外，参议院战场上还有一场大型辩论之夜。</description><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 23:24:14 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/08/us/politics/trump-republican-voters.html</guid></item><item><title>肯·帕克斯顿在德克萨斯州参议员竞选中向谁寻求帮助？</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/07/us/politics/ken-paxton-texas-senate-race.html</link><description>特朗普今晚将在德克萨斯州为参议院候选人进行竞选活动。</description><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 22:56:44 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/07/us/politics/ken-paxton-texas-senate-race.html</guid></item><item><title>由于这些选民群体，民主党在民意调查中看起来很强大</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/06/us/politics/democrats-senate-polls-voters.html</link><description>不同的集团正在向左移动。他们可以左右关键的参议院竞选。</description><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 22:39:50 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/06/us/politics/democrats-senate-polls-voters.html</guid></item><item><title>对共和党感到不满的拉美裔选民可能会决定中期选举</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/02/us/politics/midterms-hispanic-voters-trump.html</link><description>拉美裔选民对共和党越来越不满。原因如下。</description><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 21:38:35 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/02/us/politics/midterms-hispanic-voters-trump.html</guid></item><item><title>特朗普在跨越共和党据点的中期巡演中进行辩护</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/30/us/politics/trump-midterms-oklahoma-alabama-nebraska.html</link><description>一些深红色区域需要震动。</description><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:54:34 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/30/us/politics/trump-midterms-oklahoma-alabama-nebraska.html</guid></item><item><title>最新中期民意调查显示共和党的亮点</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/25/us/politics/republicans-midterms-senate-polls.html</link><description>我们的新民意调查显示，缅因州出现了好转。</description><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 22:12:54 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/25/us/politics/republicans-midterms-senate-polls.html</guid></item><item><title>心脏地带的麻烦</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/23/us/politics/midwest-republican-candidates-trump.html</link><description>由于天然气价格居高不下，共和党在所谓的“蓝墙”州及其他地区处于守势。</description><pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 22:24:48 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/23/us/politics/midwest-republican-candidates-trump.html</guid></item><item><title>中期选举前的经济状况：通胀上升和人工智能的不安</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/21/us/politics/midterm-elections-economy.html</link><description>为什么目前的情况感觉如此奇怪，以及这在 11 月意味着什么。</description><pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 22:28:35 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/21/us/politics/midterm-elections-economy.html</guid></item><item><title>选民称共和党现在是“精英”政党</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/18/us/politics/republicans-elitist-party-voters-poll.html</link><description>我们采访了对特朗普感到不满的独立人士。</description><pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 22:16:17 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/18/us/politics/republicans-elitist-party-voters-poll.html</guid></item><item><title>这是中期冲刺指南</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/16/us/politics/trump-midterms-senate-map.html</link><description>我们分析一下比赛的状况。</description><pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 23:00:20 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/16/us/politics/trump-midterms-senate-map.html</guid></item></channel></rss>